Everything outside docs/upstream/ was written for this team.

docs/upstream/ contains text-only copies of third-party documentation, kept for offline use inside
the team. The content is unchanged. Some folders were converted to Markdown (includes inlined,
placeholders filled in): the MongoDB, Cassandra, Elasticsearch / Kibana 8.19, Elasticsearch 9.5 and
Redis Enterprise docs. Each folder keeps its own license:

- Each folder's LICENSE file (copied from the source repository), when the repository has one.
- docs/upstream/VERSIONS.md lists every folder's source repository, commit and license.

The MongoDB documentation folders (mongodb-manual-*, ops-manager-*, mck-*, mongosh,
mongodb-database-tools) come from github.com/mongodb/docs, licensed under Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/),
as stated in that repository's README.

The Dell Container Storage Modules folder (dell-csm-powerflex) comes from github.com/dell/csm-docs,
licensed under the Apache License 2.0, as stated in that repository's README.

The Elastic 9.x guides folder (elastic-9-guides) comes from github.com/elastic/docs-content, licensed
under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0. Because that license allows no
derivatives, those files are kept exactly as published (no conversion).

The Redis Enterprise folder (redis-enterprise-software) comes from github.com/redis/docs, licensed under
Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0.
